{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.centralC2_coeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.centralC2_coeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyCoeff.lean#L92-L119","doc":"**Identity (B), ℂ-free computational core, fully discharged.** The Jucys–Murphy central\nelement `C₂ = Σ_k X_k²` with `X_k = Σ_{i<k}(i k)` has identity coefficient `\\binom{n}{2}` in\n`R[S_n] = MonoidAlgebra R (Perm (Fin n))`, over **any** `CommRing R` — no ℂ, no representation\ntheory, no `dim(λ)`/SYT/RSK. Per-`k`: `coeff_1(X_k²) = #{i<k} = k` (`jm_swap_sq_coeff_one` +\n`Finset.Iio` card); summing: `Σ_{k} k = \\binom{n}{2}` (Gauss). This is the exact `\\binom{n}{2}`\nof `IdentityIContentDecomposition.jm_identity_coeff_two` on main, now realised as the\ngroup-algebra coefficient itself. The remaining bridge to `Σ_λ dim(λ)²·Σ_c c(c)²` is the\nstandard regular-rep/Wedderburn step over **ℚ** (S_n rational), not ℂ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.jm_swap_sq_coeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.jm_swap_sq_coeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyCoeff.lean#L78-L90","doc":"**Jucys–Murphy building block.** For any finite `t ⊆ Fin n`, the JM-style sum\n`Σ_{i∈t} (i k)` (transpositions all sharing the strand `k`) has squared identity coefficient\n`|t|`. The map `i ↦ (i k)` is globally injective (`(i k)` sends `k ↦ i`, so it determines `i`)\nand each `(i k)` is an involution, so the indexed lemma applies. With `t = {i : i < k}` this is\n`coeff_1(X_k²) = #{i < k} = k`; summing over `k` gives `coeff_1(Σ_k X_k²) = \\binom{n}{2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.coeff_one_sq_sum_single_involution_indexed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.coeff_one_sq_sum_single_involution_indexed","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyCoeff.lean#L64-L76","doc":"**Indexed form** (what the Jucys–Murphy element plugs into directly). For an *injective*\nfamily `f` of involutions indexed by a finite set `t`, the identity coefficient of\n`(Σ_{i∈t} f i)²` is `|t|`. Re-index the core lemma through `t.image f` (injective ⇒ card `|t|`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.coeff_one_sq_sum_single_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff.coeff_one_sq_sum_single_involution","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JucysMurphyCoeff.lean#L40-L62","doc":"**ℂ-free core of Identity (B).** In `R[G] = MonoidAlgebra R G` over any `CommRing R`, the\nidentity coefficient of `(Σ_{g∈s} g)²` is `|s|` whenever every `g ∈ s` is an involution\n(`g·g = 1`). Proof: expand the square to `Σ_{g,h} single (g·h) 1`; evaluating at `1` keeps the\nterms with `g·h = 1`, i.e. `h = g⁻¹ = g` (involution), so exactly the `|s|` diagonal terms\nsurvive, each contributing `1`. No field, no representation theory — pure group-algebra\ncombinatorics over generic `R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}